      "section": "Splice junctions",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "A sashimi plot: per sample, read coverage as bars and every splice junction as a dome from donor to acceptor, its height and width set by the reads crossing it. In the knockdowns the dome from exon 2 straight to exon 4 rises while coverage over exon 3 drops: that exon is skipped. Drag or scroll to zoom, raise Min reads to hide weak junctions, switch to Arcs for the Plotly panel. Inputs are STAR SJ.out.tab junctions plus binned coverage, as written by nf-core/rnaseq, rnafusion and nanoseq (synthetic exons placed in CHD4, hg38).\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
